  "raw_input": "When did the first bank come into existence that is part of an organization that serves rural areas of India with basic banking and financial services?",
  "ground_truth": "on 20 July 2009",
  "final_output": "The first bank in India that was established to serve rural areas with basic banking and financial services was the **Punjab National Bank (Punjab National Bank)**, but more specifically, the **Regional Rural Banks (RRBs)** were established to serve rural areas. The first Regional Rural Bank was established in **1975** — the **Durgapur Regional Rural Bank** — under the Regional Rural Banks Act, 1976. However, the first bank specifically created to serve rural India was the **Punjab, Sind, Sindh and Gujarat (PSSG) Regional Rural Bank**, which was established in **1975**.\n\nBut the most accurate and widely recognized answer is that the **first bank established specifically to serve rural India** was the **Punjab National Bank's rural outreach**, though the formal institutional structure began with the **Regional Rural Banks**.\n\nThus, the first bank part of an organization serving rural India with basic banking and financial services came into existence in **1975** with the establishment of the first Regional Rural Bank.\n\n✅ Final Answer: **1975**.",
